-- erwartet: C001
-- **Pointer arithmetic, `+` on a pointer.** `SPRACHE.md` §5.2 gives computed
-- addresses exactly one form -- `place[expr]` with a bounded index -- and
-- `p + 1` is not it: the sum of an address and a number is no address any
-- region check ever covered. Against the unchanged tree the checker types the
-- sum as unknown and stays silent (`0 errors`), and the emitter lowers it to
-- C pointer arithmetic (`q = p + 1`), which computes exactly the uncovered
-- address. The rule this probe pairs with (p03) refuses the shape at the
-- emission site by name (`C001`); this file pins what it must catch.
-- The twin `p[1]` is the admitted index form and stays silent.
--
-- Measured 2026-09-11 against the unchanged checker+emitter: falls with
-- nothing -- red until the rule lands, green with it (integrator reconciles).
module gift::pointer_arith_plus_refused {

type Text = { n : u32, };

impl fn weiter(p : ptr<user, rw> Text)
    effects { writes p }
    costs <= 8 ops
{
    p[1].n = 2;
    let q = p + 1;
}

}
